{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the fugitive came.</b> This is Og, who escaped from the Flood, and Abraham elevated his name ('Og') because when he came before him Sarah was busy with cakes (עוגות); therefore Moses feared lest this merit stand for Og his son, who was king of Bashan — and all the more so if this was literally Og, according to the view of our Rabbis of blessed memory, that he was so very large and lived long until the time of Moses." "<b>And in the Midrash</b> of Pirkei R. Eliezer: 'And the fugitive came' — this is Michael, and he is the fugitive spoken of in Ezekiel, as it is written of him (Ezekiel 33:21): ״בא אלי הפליט מירושלים״." "<b>And he dwelt in the terebinths of Mamre the Amorite.</b> It is known that Abraham's three friends — Aner, Eshcol, and Mamre — were Amorites, but we do not find in Scripture that it calls any one of them 'Amorite' except Mamre alone, nor do we find this mentioned in any other place except here. The reason is that Scripture mentions the covenant, so that you should not understand, when it says 'and they were Abram's allies,' that all three gave Abraham the counsel of circumcision — for none gave him this counsel except Mamre alone, as our Rabbis of blessed memory mentioned. Therefore it says 'the Amorite,' from the root of אמירה (saying), for he said to him: 'What — if the Holy One, blessed be He, sought your very life, would you not surrender it to Him? How much more so one limb!' and furthermore: 'Who saved you from the kings and from the famine, and who saved you from Ur of the Chaldees — how much more so will He save you now!' And this is the meaning of ממר\"א as a notaricon: מ(לכים) מ(ילה) ר(עבון) א(ש). And we find the language of אמירה in connection with the commandment of circumcision (Psalms 119:162): ״שש אנכי על אמרתך״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:22.550234204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}